# AssetHealthIndex

Production-ready modular Python implementation of an Asset Health Index (AHI) workflow inspired by Han et al. (2023), combining a BP Neural Network (`MLPClassifier`) and Mahalanobis Distance.

## Features

- Data validation: schema, missing values, duplicates, datatypes, ranges, quality report
- Preprocessing: imputation, outlier clipping, normalization + `StandardScaler`
- BP Neural Network training/evaluation (60/40 stratified split)
- Healthy baseline (mean/covariance/inverse covariance)
- Mahalanobis Distance batch scoring with covariance regularization
- Health Index (HI) and AHI (0-100)
- Rules-engine-based health classification
- CSV/JSON outputs, trend dataset, and Power BI-ready dataset
- Explainable maintenance recommendations

## Install

```bash
pip install -e .[dev]
```

## Run

```bash
ahi-pipeline --input /absolute/path/to/data.csv --config config/default.yaml --output-dir artifacts
```

Input columns:

- `timestamp`
- `asset_id`
- `speed`
- `frequency`
- `voltage`
- `current`
- `active_power`
- `reactive_power`
- `power_factor`
- `label`
